bound-lock/1 about="Unsigned proposed research statement; native reader capture and admitted closure pending." at=witness:042/joint-forms-phase by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=test/t38-forms.test.ts|vectors/laws/t38/circle12.json|vectors/laws/t38/halfplanes.json role=writes scope=obligations/theory/T38 value="For closed real intervals, pairwise nonempty intersections suffice for finite families; this is not a claim about every lattice form. Convex sets in R^d require the hypotheses of Helly and witnesses up to d+1. A three-arc discrete circle and fixed halfplanes distinguish two- and three-member empty meets."
bound-lock/1 about="Unsigned proposed research statement; native reader capture and admitted closure pending." at=witness:042/joint-forms-phase by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=vectors/laws/t38/circle12.json|test/t38-forms.test.ts role=writes scope=obligations/theory/F2 value="On twelve discrete points, five-point arcs starting at 0, 4 and 8 meet in every pair and not jointly. This finite example does not prove the absence of every finite Helly bound."
bound-lock/1 about="Unsigned proposed research statement; native reader capture and admitted closure pending." at=witness:042/joint-forms-phase by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=vectors/laws/t38/halfplanes.json|test/t38-forms.test.ts role=writes scope=obligations/theory/F3 value="The four seller/buyer/carrier/auditor halfplanes conflict with seller/auditor witness; x>=0,y>=0,x+y<=-1 is pairwise consistent and jointly empty. Fixed nonnegative certificates verify these finite cases only."
bound-lock/1 about="Unsigned proposed research statement; native reader capture and admitted closure pending." at=witness:042/joint-forms-phase by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=vectors/laws/t87/phase-controls.json|samples/laws/t87/phase-domain.json|test/measures/t87-phase.test.ts role=writes scope=obligations/theory/F4 value="Under the provisional integer domain p divides n and 0<=s<p, RI=log2(n/p)-h(s/p). For n=12,p=4, the controls at s=0,1,2,3 are 1.584962500721156,0.7736843762620231,0.5849625007211561,0.7736843762620231 bits. Halfphase is one bit below inphase. Author domain confirmation and worst-case objective remain open."
bound-lock/1 about="Unsigned proposed research statement; native reader capture and admitted closure pending." at=witness:042/joint-forms-phase by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=test/measures/t87-phase.test.ts role=writes scope=obligations/theory/T87 value="The raw absolute-angle criterion is not invariant under adding a full turn: phases 0 and 2pi reinforce. Existing cancels uses cos of the difference. This distinguishes a missing wrapped-distance hypothesis; it does not infer laminarity or a near-phase RI worst-case objective."
bound-lock/1 about="Unsigned proposed research statement; native reader capture and admitted closure pending." at=witness:042/joint-forms-phase by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=vectors/laws/f1/finite-arithmetic.json|test/t38-forms.test.ts role=writes scope=obligations/theory/F1 value="For n=3..7, arithmetic reproduces the provided log2(n)-2+2/n values and Bell squared pair counts. No exhaustive partition enumeration, general optimality proof or independent browser/WebAssembly-origin verification was performed."
bound-lock/1 about="Folding claims is union in the knowledge order; arrival order never decides." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/L1 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="For intervals of a lattice, pairs suffice: every conflict has a witness of two (Helly number 2). Convex forms in\n   R^d need witnesses up to d+1 (d=2 → 3). Cyclic forms (phase) without a declared cut have no finite Helly number;\n   with a declared cut, h=2 on arcs not crossing it. Shannon partitions have no finite Helly number." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/L2 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Excluding any value from the maximal coincidence may exclude the truth; keeping the fork is the only correct action." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/L3 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Each entering origin closes bits and spends confidence; the guarantee of the meet is 1 − Σp UNDER DECLARED,\n   JUSTIFIED failure probabilities p_i; if Σp ≥ 1 the bound is trivial and must be reported as such. Agreement\n   and copy count do not estimate p." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/L4 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="In the Shannon lattice, shared information may have no carrier: at most log₂n − 2 + 2/n bits." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/L5 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Information about the truth is bounded by the structure of causes, not by the number of witnesses; copies do not add." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/L6 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="A closed group cannot measure its own reliability: for a cause covering all witnesses, P(unanimity on v) = c/n\n   for every accuracy q, so q is unidentifiable from inside." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/L7 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Only dissent identifies what origins share; unanimity says nothing. For a partial cause, q is identified iff an\n   outsider exists with error p ≠ (n−1)/n. Rank-breaking structures: same-set factors, singleton factors,\n   cycle-covering factors, more factors than pairs." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/L8 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Which parameters can be measured is known before observing, from the pairs matrix of declared causes." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/L9 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Extremal: over n equiprobable states, max RI(x,y) = log₂n − 2 + 2/n, attained only by the path on n+1 vertices\n   (x groups edges by even endpoint, y by odd). Proof chain: lem-phi (φ(t) ≥ 2(t−1)) → lem-merge → lem-identity →\n   lem-join → lem-meet → thm-extremal. Enumeration n=3..7: 0.251629, 0.500000, 0.721928, 0.918296, 1.093069;\n   pair counts 25, 225, 2704, 41209, 769129 (Bell numbers squared → complete)." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/F1 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Circle of 12 points, arcs of length 5 starting at 0, 4, 8: every pair meets, the three do not." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/F2 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Half-plane claims x+y≤12 (seller), x≥3 (buyer), y≥2 (carrier), x+y≥14 (auditor): CONFLICT, witness\n   {seller, auditor}, 2 of 4. Minimal example needing three: x ≥ 0, y ≥ 0, x + y ≤ −1 (pairwise consistent,\n   jointly empty). Both go in as vectors." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/F3 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Phase: RI = log₂(n/p) − h(s/p) with n states, period p dividing n, shift s with 0 ≤ s < p, h the binary entropy;\n   worst case is near-phase, not anti-phase. (Author to confirm the domain; until then the vector carries these\n   hypotheses explicitly.)" at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/F4 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="M/4: with a common cause c of accuracy q, C = log₂n − c·[h(q) + (1−q)·log₂(n−1)]; dissent\n   d = (1−c)·[1 − (1−p)² − p²/(n−1)]. Sample n=4, c=1/5: one covering factor q=0 → 1.683 bits; {A,B},{A,B} → 1.430;\n   {A,B},{C,D} → 1.937; triangle {A,B},{B,C},{A,C} → 1.835; q=1/2 → 1.642. Numeric policy: binary64-log2.\n   Negative sample (each a named refusal): missing q → refuse; 2 witnesses requesting c → unmeasured; 3 binary\n   witnesses → unmeasured; perfect agreement → no-dissent; copies → same bound; partial governance → unmeasured.\n   HOW FACTORS GOVERN in duplicated/disjoint/triangle models is NOT fully specified: region stays open (§5)." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/F5 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Obligations: a cell may declare names it needs; an obligation is an open region of form bytes inside the cell\n   (not an edge). Bytes hashing to the name narrow it to a point; received bytes are themselves a cell whose open\n   regions fold inside the parent's. Terminates: the knowledge order is well-founded, plus an instruction budget." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/P1 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Byte regions: open / resolved / fork (two holders, two byte sets: both kept) / unmet (no holder: stop, name it).\n   Wrong bytes are refused, never patched." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/P2 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Named core: a result declares the names it depends on; validity is a function of that core only." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/P3 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Root as a cell of names: a list of names folds into one name. Atoms (form bytes) have no dissent; dissent lives\n   in claims. The atom zero (fold/hash/assemble) is trusted out of band; in Bound it is the WebAssembly kernel." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/P4 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Name in the fragment: a link carries #form:hash, not a place; the form is in the name because it declares how\n   claims combine (Helly order). Expected addresses: hash(\"answer to claim X\") is known before the answer exists." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/P5 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Paper as holder: a QR holds a name or small bytes (one QR 2,953 B; A4 sheet ≈140 KB); two tiers of \"belongs to\n   no one\": complete-on-paper, and named (bytes exist while someone keeps them)." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/P6 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Copresence: commit-reveal; horizon ≥ max latency; decisions with duration; actions as intervals." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/P7 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Fold-as-you-go: resolve by frontier, by need, by proximity." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/P8 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Universality test: a primitive enters only if it means the same in a game, a news story and a sensor without\n   code change. Never in a contract: ticks, demos, games, pages, APIs." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/P9 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Derived regions: form=derived, value = f(named regions), closing policy eager|deferred (from Scion's derived\n   data; passes P9). Verification is a claim, not a gate: implementation claims fold immediately; verification is\n   a derived region closed later. Cost of folding a cell ∝ the cell, never the world." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/P10 value=lock
